  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-IADB" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-American Development Bank</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa de Apoyo al Sector Transporte I</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Transportation Sector I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">La operacin propuesta constituye el primer prstamo del Banco al Programa de Apoyo al Sector Transporte (programa) cuya estructura apunta a que los recursos del Banco puedan ser aportados de forma modular en los aos 2010, 2011 y 2012. Cada operacin que conforma el programa ser sometida individualmente a consideracin del Directorio del Banco, comprendiendo inversiones que se justifiquen y sean viables en forma autnoma, pero que permitan ir alcanzando metas integrales para el sector de forma acumulativa. El programa tiene por objetivo general contribuir a mejorar la eficiencia del transporte terrestre por carreteras en Nicaragua, a fin de estimular la actividad econmica y el bienestar de la poblacin, y facilitar la integracin de las diferentes regiones del pascon el resto de Centroamrica. Los objetivos especficos del programa son: (i) reducir los costos de operacin vehicular; (ii) aumentar las velocidades de circulacin; (iii) reducir las interrupciones al trnsito; (iv) reducir la accidentalidad; y (v) fomentar la conservacin del patrimonio vial.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed operation is the Banks first loan for the Transport Sector Support Program, whereby Bank funds may be provided in a modular manner in the years 2010, 2011 and 2012. Each operation in the program will be submitted individually to the Banks Board of Executive Directors for consideration, and will comprise investments that have their own rationale and feasibility while allowing comprehensive targets to be achieved for the sector cumulatively. The general objective of the program is to make road transport in Nicaragua more efficient in order to stimulate economic activity and contribute to the well-being of the population, while facilitating integration of the countrys regions with the rest of Central America. The specific objectives are: (i) to reduce vehicle operating costs; (ii) to increase travel speeds; (iii) to reducedisruptions to transit; (iv) to reduce accident rates; and (v) to foster conservation of road infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
